      "content": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <memory>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nclass FastScanner {\n    static const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\n    int idx;\n    int size;\npublic:\n    FastScanner() : idx(0), size(0) {}\n    inline int getChar() {\n        if (idx >= size) {\n            size = (int)fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n            idx = 0;\n            if (size == 0) return -1;\n        }\n        return (unsigned char)buf[idx++];\n    }\n    inline int nextInt() {\n        int c = getChar();\n        while (c <= ' ' && c != -1) c = getChar();\n        int sign = 1;\n        if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\n        int x = 0;\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n            c = getChar();\n        }\n        return sign * x;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    std::unique_ptr<int[]> mat(new int[(size_t)n * n]);\n    std::vector<long long> colsum(n, 0);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        size_t base = (size_t)i * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int v = fs.nextInt();\n            mat[base + j] = v;\n            if (i < s) colsum[j] += v;\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long best = LLONG_MIN;\n\n    // top row of the window is 0\n    long long cur = 0;\n    for (int r = 0; r < s; ++r) cur += colsum[r];\n    if (cur > best) best = cur;\n    for (int right = s; right < n; ++right) {\n        cur += colsum[right] - colsum[right - s];\n        if (cur > best) best = cur;\n    }\n\n    const int lastTop = n - s;\n    for (int top = 1; top <= lastTop; ++top) {\n        const int* oldRow = mat.get() + (size_t)(top - 1) * n;\n        const int* newRow = mat.get() + (size_t)(top + s - 1) * n;\n\n        long long cur2 = 0;\n        for (int r = 0; r < s; ++r) {\n            colsum[r] += (long long)newRow[r] - oldRow[r];\n            cur2 += colsum[r];\n        }\n        if (cur2 > best) best = cur2;\n        for (int right = s; right < n; ++right) {\n            colsum[right] += (long long)newRow[right] - oldRow[right];\n            cur2 += colsum[right] - colsum[right - s];\n            if (cur2 > best) best = cur2;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", best);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replacing the snake O(S*N^2) traversal and vector-of-vectors layout with a contiguous flat matrix, an O(N^2) vertical column-sum sliding window, and combining row updates with horizontal max scans in one pass improves cache locality and reduces memory traffic.",
  "notes": "Uses a buffered integer scanner to reduce I/O overhead, stores the matrix contiguously for sequential access, and computes each new top-row window by updating column sums while simultaneously scanning horizontally, avoiding repeated strided accesses. Intermediate sums use long long for safety; final result is printed as required.",
